<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n104056" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τῑτάν</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾶνος</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ὁ</span>; mostly pl.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τῑτᾶνες</span>, 
			Ep.
		 and 
			Ion.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τῑτῆνες, οἱ</span>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>the Titans</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				14.279
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Ap.</u>
				335
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				630
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Cratin.
			</span></i> in <i><span class="en">
				<u>PSI</u>
				11
			</span></i>. 
			<i><span class="en">
				1212.11
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				19
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τ. Προμηθεύς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OC</u>
					56
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				1122
			</span></i>; of Atlas, dub. in <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				427
			</span></i> (lyr.); of the Sun-god, <i><span class="en">
				Emp.
				38
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ezek.
				<u>Exag.</u>
				217
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Orph.
				<u>A.</u>
				512
			</span></i>; of Apollo, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12(5).893.1
			</span></i> (Tenos, dub. l.), <i><span class="en">
				9(1).882.4
			</span></i> (Corc.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Schwyzer</u>
				649.8
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Balbilla</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τιτάν: παιδεραστής</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> a kind of
			<i>comet</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Heph.Astr.
				1.24
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Lyd.
				<u>Ost.</u>
				p.169
			</span></i>). (Derived by <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				207
			</span></i> sqq. partly from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τιταίνω</span>
				(<i>the Strivers</i>), partly from the root of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίσις </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Οὐρανὸς . .
				φάσκε δὲ τιταίνοντας ἀτασθαλίῃ μέγα ῥέξαι ἔργον,
				τοῖο δ᾽ ἔπειτα τίσιν μετόπισθεν ἔσεσθαι</span>); the
			latter derivation also in <i><span class="en">
				Orph.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				57
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.996c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, in modified form. Perh. really connected with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίταξ</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βασιλεύς</span>
			, and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τιτήνη</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βασιλίς</span>
			 in <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>)</div>
